/**
 * Grade 7 informational articles: 50 of them, five for each of RI.7.1 to
 * RI.7.10, alternating science and social studies.
 *
 * Held to the bands in scripts/reading-article-plan.json: seven paragraphs,
 * a higher version at LL 1040-1130 and a lower one at LL 820-920 with the
 * same lettered paragraphs, five questions of the five named kinds.
 *
 * What changes at grade 7, and why the topics are chosen the way they are:
 * the standards stop asking what a text says and start asking how it was
 * built. RI.7.8 wants a child to judge whether evidence is sufficient, and
 * RI.7.9 wants them to notice that two writers chose different evidence.
 * An article that only reports cannot carry that work, so each one here is
 * picked for having a visible seam -- a claim that was contested, a number
 * that had to be argued for, two records that disagree.
 *
 *   bun run scripts/articles/g7.src.mjs && bun run scripts/merge-articles.mjs
 *   bun run scripts/check-articles.mjs
 */
