      "The argument against is that a camera is not a window. Coverage is edited. The minute chosen for a bulletin is chosen because something happened. A trial is mostly hours of procedure.",
      "There is also an effect on the room. Lawyers, witnesses and judges behave differently when recorded. A system that needs candid testimony has reason to worry.",
      "Courts have settled this differently. Some allow cameras. Some allow audio only. Some allow sketch artists and nothing more. Each rule judges which record does least harm.",
